      "writtenOn": "2017-11-14T23:58:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, since RefcountedResource does not have access to any implementor details, why do we need generics at all? What if RefcountedResource just had a member variable of type IResource?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 135,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 135,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "1dba141a37ec855aba076e6f1e16f5dec40e5d48",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c6c21545_bbd81aed",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/IpSecService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 135,
      "author": {
        "id": 1221725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-15T20:23:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The generics allow the getResource() method to return the correct type, so we don\u0027t have to cast it afterwards.\n\nie, if we just had a RefcountedResource wrapping an SPI using a field of type IResource, if we wanted to access the SPI\u0027s remote address, we would do:\n\n((SpiRecord)refcountedResource.getResource()).mRemoteAddress; // must be casted from IResource to SpiRecord\n\nOn the other hand, using generics, we can do: \n\nrefcountedResource.getResource().mRemoteAddress; // without the cast",
      "parentUuid": "aacb8909_10611040",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 135,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 135,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "1dba141a37ec855aba076e6f1e16f5dec40e5d48",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
